   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 549 of the laws of 2005 amending the tax law relating\nto authorizing the county of Herkimer to impose a county recording tax on\nobligation secured by a mortgage on real property, in relation to extending\nthe effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5607",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5607-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 549 of 2005",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5607\n\nSPONSOR: WALCZYK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 549 of the laws of 2005 amending the tax law\nrelating to authorizing the county of Herkimer to impose a county\nrecording tax on obligation secured by a mortgage on real property, in\nrelation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nExtends authorization of the county of Herkimer to impose a county\nrecording tax on obligation secured by a mortgage on real property.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Section 2 of chapter 549 of the laws of 2005 amending the\ntax law relating to authorizing the county of Herkimer to impose a coun-\nty recording tax on obligation secured by a mortgage on real property,\nin relation to extending the effectiveness thereof as amended by chapter\n332 of the laws of 2023.\n\nSection 2 - Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe county of Herkimer has requested this legislation to extend their\nauthority to impose a mortgage recording tax in the amount of twenty-\nfive cents for each one hundred dollars, until December 1, 2027.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
